## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates practical data protection across SAP on AWS with Snowflake analytics, balancing real-time access and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- SAP S/4HANA data ingestion and masking
- Field-level masking rules for PII
- Snowflake masking policies and data sharing
- AWS KMS key management and IAM governance
- Auditing, rollback, and failover strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example masking function
function maskPII(record) {
  const r = {...record};
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{2}).+(@.*)/, '$1***$2');
  if (r.phone) r.phone = r.phone.replace(/(\d{3})\d{4}(\d{3})/, '$1***$2');
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-' + r.ssn.slice(-4);
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate masking without leaking data in logs?
- How would you rotate keys and propagate policy changes across Snowflake without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a cross-account, auditable backup strategy for SAP HANA on EC2 that enforces immutability and cross-account access control.

## Key Concepts

- Immutable backups with S3 Object Lock (COMPLIANCE)
- Cross-account IAM roles and trust policies
- KMS CMK grants for cross-account encryption/decryption
- AWS Backup vault policies and cross-account access
- S3 bucket versioning and access policies

## Code Example

```hcl
# Terraform snippet: immutable SAP backups with cross-account access
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "sap_backups" {
  bucket = "sap-backups-prod"
  acl    = "private"

  versioning {
    enabled = true
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_object_lock_configuration" "lock" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.sap_backups.id
  object_lock_enabled = true

  rule {
    default_retention {
      mode = "COMPLIANCE"
      days = 3650
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "sap_backup_cross_account_role" {
  name = "sap-backup-cross-account-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow",
      Principal = {
        AWS = "arn:aws:iam::BACKUP_ACCOUNT_ID:root"
      },
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate the CMK without service disruption?
- How would you validate backups remain immutable after policy changes?
